cal staging","crown":"crown: an ornamental jeweled headdress signifying sovereignty","desert":"desert: arid land with little or no vegetation","diamond":"diamond: a transparent piece of diamond that has been cut and polished and is valued as a precious gem","dinosaur":"dinosaur: any of numerous extinct terrestrial reptiles of the Mesozoic era","doctor":"doctor: a licensed medical practitioner","dragon":"dragon: a creature of Teutonic mythology; usually represented as breathing fire and having a reptilian body and sometimes wings","dream":"dream: a series of mental images and emotions occurring during sleep","earthquake":"earthquake: shaking and vibration at the surface of the earth resulting from underground movement along a fault plane or from volcanic activity","engine":"engine: motor that converts thermal energy to mechanical work","feather":"feather: branching, hair-like structure that grows on the bodies of birds","festival":"festival: a day or period of time set aside for feasting and celebration","fireplace":"fireplace: an open recess in a wall at the base of a chimney where a fire can be built","forest":"forest: the trees and other plants in a large densely wooded area","fountain":"fountain: a structure from which an artificially produced jet of water arises","garden":"garden: a plot of ground where plants are cultivated","ghost":"ghost: the visible disembodied soul of a dead person","glacier":"glacier: a slowly moving mass of ice","guitar":"guitar: a stringed instrument usually having six strings; played by strumming or plucking","harbour":"harbour: a sheltered port where ships can take on or discharge cargo","helmet":"helmet: armor plate that protects the head","honey":"honey: a sweet yellow liquid produced by bees","hospital":"hospital: a health facility where patients receive treatment","island":"island: a land mass (smaller than a continent) that is surrounded by water","jungle":"jungle: an impenetrable equatorial forest","kettle":"kettle: a metal pot for stewing or boiling; usually has a lid","kingdom":"kingdom: the domain ruled by a king or queen","ladder":"ladder: steps consisting of two parallel members connected by rungs; for climbing up or down","lantern":"lantern: light in a transparent protective case","library":"library: a room where books are kept","lighthouse":"lighthouse: a tower with a light that gives warning of shoals to passing ships","lightning":"lightning: abrupt electric discharge from cloud to cloud or from cloud to earth accompanied by the emission of light","market":"market: the world of commercial activity where goods and services are bought and sold","mirror":"mirror: polished surface that forms images by reflecting light","moon":"moon: any natural satellite of a planet","mountain":"mountain: a land mass that projects well above its surroundings; higher than a hill","museum":"museum: a depository for collecting and displaying objects having scientific or historical or artistic value","music":"music: an artistic form of auditory communication incorporating instrumental or vocal tones in a structured and continuous manner","ocean":"ocean: a large body of water constituting a principal part of the hydrosphere","orchard":"orchard: land planted with fruit trees such as apple and pear trees","painting":"painting: graphic art consisting of an artistic composition made by applying paints to a surface","passport":"passport: a document issued by a country to a citizen allowing that person to travel abroad and re-enter the home country","piano":"piano: a keyboard instrument that is played by depressing keys that cause hammers to strike tuned strings and produce sounds","picnic":"picnic: a day devoted to an outdoor social gathering","pirate":"pirate: someone who robs at sea or plunders the land from the sea without having a commission from any sovereign nation","planet":"planet: (astronomy) any of the nine large celestial bodies in the solar system that revolve around the sun and shine by reflected light; Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune, and Pluto in order of their proximity to the sun; viewed from the constellation Hercules, all the planets rotate around the sun in a counterclockwise direction","prison":"prison: a correctional institution where persons are confined while on trial or for punishment","rainbow":"rainbow: an arc of colored light in the sky caused by refraction of the sun's rays by rain","river":"river: a large natural stream of water (larger than a creek)","robot":"robot: a mechanism that can move automatically","rocket":"rocket: any vehicle self-propelled by a rocket engine","sandwich":"sandwich: two (or more) slices of bread with a filling between them","school":"school: an educational institution","shadow":"shadow: shade within clear boundaries","ship":"ship: a vessel that carries passengers or freight","snowman":"snowman: a person-shaped figure built from snow, often with a carrot nose, hat, and scarf","stadium":"stadium: a large structure for open-air sports or entertainments","storm":"storm: a violent weather condition with winds 64-72 knots (11 on the Beaufort scale) and precipitation and thunder and lightning","submarine":"submarine: a submersible warship usually armed with torpedoes","sunrise":"sunrise: the first light of day","telescope":"telescope: a magnifier of images of distant objects","theatre":"theatre: a building where theatrical performances or motion-picture shows can be presented","thunder":"thunder: a deep prolonged loud noise","tiger":"tiger: large feline of forests in most of Asia having a tawny coat with black stripes; endangered","tower":"tower: a structure taller than its diameter; can stand alone or be attached to a larger building","train":"train: public transport provided by a line of railway cars coupled together and drawn by a locomotive","treasure":"treasure: accumulated wealth in the form of money or jewels etc.","tunnel":"tunnel: a passageway through or under something, usually underground (especially one for trains or cars)","umbrella":"umbrella: a lightweight handheld collapsible canopy","village":"village: a community of people smaller than a town","volcano":"volcano: a fissure in the earth's crust (or in the surface of some other planet) through which molten lava and gases erupt","waterfall":"waterfall: a steep descent of the water of a river","wedding":"wedding: the social event at which the ceremony of marriage is performed","whistle":"whistle: a small wind instrument that produces a whistling sound by blowing into it","window":"window: a framework of wood or metal that contains a glass windowpane and is built into a wall or roof to admit light or air","winter":"winter: the coldest season of the year; in the Northern Hemisphere it extends from the winter solstice to the vernal equinox","wizard":"wizard: one who practices magic or sorcery","accordion":"accordion: a portable box-shaped free-reed instrument; the reeds are made to vibrate by air from the bellows controlled by the player","adventure":"adventure: a wild and exciting undertaking (not necessarily lawful)","ambulance":"ambulance: a vehicle that takes people to and from hospitals","angel":"angel: spiritual being attendant upon God","ant":"ant: social insect living in organized colonies; characteristically the males and fertile queen have wings during breeding season; wingless sterile females are the workers","apartment":"apartment: a suite of rooms usually on one floor of an apartment house","archer":"archer: a person who is expert in the use of a bow and arrow","armour":"armour: protective covering made of metal and used in combat","artist":"artist: a person whose creative work shows sensitivity and imagination","astronaut":"astronaut: a person trained to travel in a spacecraft","autumn":"autumn: the season when the leaves fall from the trees","backpack":"backpack: a bag carried by a strap on your back or shoulder","badger":"badger: sturdy carnivorous burrowing mammal with strong claws; widely distributed in the Northern Hemisphere","banana":"banana: elongated crescent-shaped yellow fruit with soft sweet flesh","bank":"bank: a financial institution that accepts deposits and channels the money into lending activities","barber":"barber: a hairdresser who cuts hair and shaves beards as a trade","barn":"barn: an outlying farm building for storing grain or animal feed and housing farm animals","basket":"basket: a container that is usually woven and has handles","bathroom":"bathroom: a room (as in a residence) containing a bathtub or shower and usually a washbasin and toilet","battery":"battery: a device that produces electricity; may have several primary or secondary cells arranged in parallel or series","battle":"battle: a hostile meeting of opposing military forces in the course of a war","bear":"bear: massive plantigrade carnivorous or omnivorous mammals with long shaggy coats and strong claws","bell":"bell: a hollow device made of metal that makes a ringing sound when struck","bench":"bench: a long seat for more than one person","bird":"bird: warm-blooded egg-laying vertebrates characterized by feathers and forelimbs modified as wings","birthday":"birthday: an anniversary of the day on which a person was born (or the celebration of it)","boat":"boat: a small vessel for travel on water","book":"book: a written work or composition that has been published (printed on pages bound together)","bottle":"bottle: a glass or plastic vessel used for storing drinks or other liquids; typically cylindrical without handles and with a narrow neck that can be plugged or capped","bowl":"bowl: a round vessel that is open at the top; used chiefly for holding grains or liquids","box":"box: a (usually rectangular) container; may have a lid","bread":"bread: food made from dough of flour or meal and usually raised with yeast or baking powder and then baked","breakfast":"breakfast: the first meal of the day (usually in the morning)","breeze":"breeze: a slight wind (usually refreshing)","brick":"brick: rectangular block of clay baked by the sun or in a kiln; used as a building or paving material","brother":"brother: a male with the same parents as someone else","brush":"brush: an implement that has hairs or bristles firmly set into a handle","bubble":"bubble: a hollow globule of gas (e.g., air or carbon dioxide)","bucket":"bucket: a roughly cylindrical vessel that is open at the top","bus":"bus: a vehicle carrying many passengers; used for public transport","cabinet":"cabinet: a piece of furniture resembling a cupboard with doors and shelves and drawers; for storage or display","cactus":"cactus: any succulent plant of the family Cactaceae native chiefly to arid regions of the New World and usually having spines","calendar":"calendar: a system of timekeeping that defines the beginning and length and divisions of the year","campfire":"campfire: a small outdoor fire for warmth or cooking (as at a camp)","canal":"canal: long and narrow strip of water made for boats or for irrigation","captain":"captain: an officer who is licensed to command a merchant ship","carpet":"carpet: floor covering consisting of a piece of thick heavy fabric (usually with nap or pile)","carrot":"carrot: deep orange edible root of the cultivated carrot plant","cartoon":"cartoon: a humorous or satirical drawing published in a newspaper or magazine","cat":"cat: feline mammal usually having thick soft fur and no ability to roar","cathedral":"cathedral: any large and important church","chair":"chair: a seat for one person, with a support for the back","chocolate":"chocolate: a food made from roasted ground cacao beans","cinema":"cinema: a theater where films are shown","clown":"clown: a person who amuses others by ridiculous behavior","coat":"coat: an outer garment that has sleeves and covers the body from shoulder down; worn outdoors","coconut":"coconut: large hard-shelled oval nut with a fibrous husk containing thick white meat surrounding a central cavity filled