nnahs of tropical Africa","glove":"glove: handwear: covers the hand and wrist","gold":"gold: a soft yellow malleable ductile (trivalent and univalent) metallic element; occurs mainly as nuggets in rocks and alluvial deposits; does not react with most chemicals but is attacked by chlorine and aqua regia","goose":"goose: web-footed long-necked typically gregarious migratory aquatic birds usually larger and less aquatic than ducks","grape":"grape: any of various juicy fruit of the genus Vitis with green or purple skins; grow in clusters","grass":"grass: narrow-leaved green herbage: grown as lawns; used as pasture for grazing animals; cut and dried as hay","hammer":"hammer: a hand tool with a heavy rigid head and a handle; used to deliver an impulsive force by striking","hamster":"hamster: short-tailed Old World burrowing rodent with large cheek pouches","hat":"hat: headdress that protects the head from bad weather; has shaped crown and usually a brim","hedgehog":"hedgehog: small nocturnal Old World mammal covered with both hair and protective spines","helicopter":"helicopter: an aircraft without wings that obtains its lift from the rotation of overhead blades","horse":"horse: solid-hoofed herbivorous quadruped domesticated since prehistoric times","hotel":"hotel: a building where travelers can pay for lodging and meals and other services","iceberg":"iceberg: a large mass of ice floating at sea; usually broken off of a polar glacier","jacket":"jacket: a short coat","jellyfish":"jellyfish: any of numerous usually marine and free-swimming coelenterates that constitute the sexually reproductive forms of hydrozoans and scyphozoans","jewel":"jewel: a precious or semiprecious stone incorporated into a piece of jewelry","journey":"journey: the act of traveling from one place to another","kangaroo":"kangaroo: any of several herbivorous leaping marsupials of Australia and New Guinea having large powerful hind legs and a long thick tail","key":"key: metal device shaped in such a 