er distances and then converts received signals back into sounds","tent":"tent: a portable shelter (usually of canvas stretched over supporting poles and fastened to the ground with ropes and pegs)","toothbrush":"toothbrush: small brush; has long handle; used to clean teeth","tornado":"tornado: a localized and violently destructive windstorm occurring over land characterized by a funnel-shaped cloud extending toward the ground","tractor":"tractor: a wheeled vehicle with large wheels; used in farming and other applications","traffic":"traffic: the aggregation of things (pedestrians or vehicles) coming and going in a particular locality during a specified period of time","trumpet":"trumpet: a brass musical instrument with a brilliant tone; has a narrow tube and a flared bell and is played by means of valves","turtle":"turtle: any of various aquatic and land reptiles having a bony shell and flipper-like limbs for swimming","unicorn":"unicorn: an imaginary creature represented as a white horse with a long horn growing from its forehead","violin":"violin: bowed stringed instrument that is the highest member of the violin family; this instrument has four strings and a hollow body and an unfretted fingerboard and is played with a bow","wallet":"wallet: a pocket-size case for holding papers and paper money","whale":"whale: a huge marine mammal that lives in the ocean and breathes through a blowhole","windmill":"windmill: a mill or turbine whose sails turn in the wind to provide power or electricity","wolf":"wolf: any of various predatory carnivorous canine mammals of North America and Eurasia that usually hunt in packs","zebra":"zebra: any of several fleet black-and-white striped African equines"},"trails":{"airport":["airport","airfield","airdrome","airstrip","aviation","airline","airliner","concourse","flight","hangar","airplane","aircraft","airbase","baggage","airfare","aeronautical","runway","jetliner","taxi","flying","gateway","station","aeroplane","seaport","airlift",